  padding:2px 7px;border-radius:var(--tx-rfull);line-height:1.6;flex-shrink:0}
.badge--owner{background:var(--tx-accent);color:var(--tx-accent-ink)}
.badge--admin{background:var(--tx-surface-3);color:var(--tx-ink-2);border:1px solid var(--tx-line-strong)}
.badge--coach{background:var(--tx-surface-2);color:var(--tx-ink-3);border:1px solid var(--tx-line)}
.badge--pending{background:transparent;color:var(--tx-warn);border:1px solid var(--tx-warn);opacity:.85}

/* Status dots */
.dot{display:inline-block;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;flex-shrink:0}
.dot--on{background:var(--tx-accent-text)}
.dot--warn{background:var(--tx-warn)}
.dot--off{background:var(--tx-ink-off)}

/* Pending-count badge inside a .tab button (Members tab) */
.tab-badge{
  display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  min-width:16px;height:16px;padding:0 4px;
  background:var(--tx-surface-3);color:var(--tx-ink-2);
  font-size:10px;font-weight:700;border-radius:var(--tx-rfull);
  line-height:1;
}
/* When the tab is selected the badge picks up the accent ink colour */
.tab[aria-selected="true"] .tab-badge{
  background:var(--tx-accent-soft);color:var(--tx-accent-text);
}

/* Team tab bar — extra breathing room above and a min-width so labels never cramp */
.team-tabs{gap:4px;margin-top:20px;overflow-x:auto;scrollbar-width:none}
.team-tabs::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
.team-tabs .tab{min-width:80px;justify-content:center}

/* Space between the tab bar and the panel content below it */
/* `.body` pays the scroll padding now that `/team` has the frame's own shape —
   `.ph` pinned, `.body` scrolling — so this is the panel's own 24 on top of the
   scroller's 20, and the tab strip sat that much further from its panel than
   every other screen's does. */
.team-panel{padding-top:4px}

/* Status chip on clients table */
.chip--sm{height:22px;padding:0 7px;font-size:11px}
.chip--active-status{background:var(--tx-accent-soft);color:var(--tx-accent-text);border-color:var(--tx-accent-line)}

/* Stack of cards */
.stack{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px}

/* kv definition list (dl wrapper for .kv rows) */
.kv-list{margin:0;padding:0}

/* Section label */
.section-label{font-size:11.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;
  text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--tx-ink-3);margin-bottom:8px}

/* Stat row */
.stat-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(140px,1fr));gap:12px}

/* Form field spacing */
.fld{margin-bottom:14px}
/* `.fld__h` WAS HERE, AND IT WAS A SECOND ANSWER TO A SOLVED QUESTION.
   §04 has drawn the hint since fields were drawn — 12px, `--tx-ink-3`,
   `line-height:1.5`, normal weight — and this override restyled it into a
   SECOND LABEL: 12.5px at 600 in `--tx-ink-2`, which is `.fld__l` exactly.
   Every hint in the application therefore rendered at the same size, the same
   weight and very nearly the same colour as the label above the control, and
   the field had two headings and no annotation.

   MEASURED on `/settings/profile`, where it is worst because the hints are
   sentences: *Personal or the name you trade under — whichever your clients
   already know. It is on every invite and receipt you send.* set two lines
   deep in 600 weight, directly under a one-word label in the same 600 weight.
   The loudest text in the field was the aside.

   `display:block` and `margin-bottom:5px` went with it and were dead anyway:
   `.fld` is `flex-direction:column` with a 6px gap, so the block was implied
   and the margin added 5px under the LAST child of every field in the app. */

.fld__note{font-size:12px;color:var(--tx-ink-3);margin-top:5px}

/* `.form-err` WAS HERE, AND IT WAS A SECOND ANSWER.
   A form-level error — the submission failed, as against `.fld__e`, which is
   one control refusing. §04 has had `.msg` / `.msg--err` for that all along and
   twenty-nine call-sites use it; this class existed only here and only for
   Team.tsx's ten. It is gone, along with the reason it appeared: `.msg` had no
   component in the catalogue, so the one screen that did not copy the markup
